# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The test suite runs on Windows as well as macOS and
# Linux, and several tests read the application's own source and data as text.
# Left to itself git would check those files out with CRLF on Windows, so a
# parser that splits on "\n", or an assertion that compares against a literal
# written here, would see something different from what the other two runners
# see -- a failure that cannot be reproduced anywhere but on the runner.
#
# The application is served as static files, so what is committed is what is
# published: normalising here also keeps the bytes a student downloads the same
# whoever committed them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
